[[Maintenance therapy in classical follicular lymphoma]]

!! Retrospective cohort

A 640-patient multicenter cohort found longer duration of response with maintenance among patients achieving PR after at least four BR cycles, but no demonstrated benefit among those achieving CR. Treatment selection and response assessment were not randomized; the findings do not establish that benefit is confined to PR or that maintenance can safely be omitted for every PET-negative CR. [[Hill et al., 2019|https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6486816/]]

Evidence reviewed September 7, 2026.
